<title>USA: Virginia 911 MW nuke returns to full power.</title>
<headline>Virginia 911 MW nuke returns to full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Virginia Power Co's 911 megawatt North Anna nuclear unit 1 returned to full power early Friday after tripping off line Wednesday, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We returned to 100 percent at 4:15 (EDT) this morning,&quot; company spokesman William Byrd said Friday.</p>
<p>The unit, located in Mineral, Va., tripped off line Wednesday in an equipment failure during routine testing.</p>
<p>&quot;We consider this incident to be over,&quot; Byrd said of repairs at the unit and the return to full output.</p>
<p>Virginia Power is a subsidiary of Dominion Resources Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
